- **CI contracts:** `wpt_diff_to_pr.py` consumes `wpt diff --format json` entries with `test`, `kind`, `status`, `counts`, `before`, `after`, `counts_before`, `counts_after` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:2; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:34-52); PR section delimited by `<!-- wpt-results-start -->` / `<!-- wpt-results-end -->`, replaced on re-runs (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:4-5; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:14-15; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:252-260); CLI `diff_file`, `--repo`, `--pr`, `--run-url`, `--areas`, `--dry-run` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:274-280), `--areas` naming the per-area subtest changes that upstream's `.github/scripts/wpt_area_changes.py` computes from the two reports (.github/scripts/wpt_area_changes.py:1-92); "PASS" and "OK" pass, listing capped at 400 lines (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:17-19; .github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:231-239); appends to `GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` and PATCHes the PR body through `gh api` (.github/scripts/wpt_diff_to_pr.py:293-308); WPT artifacts `wpt-report.json.zst` and `wpt-diff` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:52-56; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:80-87; .github/workflows/wpt-post-results.yml:22-27); `repository-dispatch` `update-results` to `DioxusLabs/blitz-wpt-results` after WPT on main, only when `github.repository == 'DioxusLabs/blitz'` (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:101-113; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:103); `.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh {leg}` — legs `fmt` · `clippy` (the workspace line, then, only when green and since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, upstream's own `cargo clippy -p blitz-dom --no-default-features --features svg,woff,accessibility,system-fonts,file-input,custom-widget --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`;
 .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:21-25) · `test` · `ci-scripts` · `build` · `msrv` (`cargo +1.91 build`) · `counter` · `wasm` · `doc` (`cargo doc --workspace --no-deps`) · `audit` (`cargo deny --locked --workspace --all-features check advisories licenses`, the whole workspace's graph, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates; `cargo deny check advisories` until then) · `a11y` (the `accessibility_hidden`, `accessibility_roles`, `focusability_updates`, `stand_keyboard`, `stand_contrast` and `stand_accessibility_ids` integration tests — six since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, three until then, widened on the founder's F4 «Расширить задание a11y (Рекомендую)» with no new job, no required status check and no `ci.yml` change, its pin `LegScriptTest.test_gate_legs_dispatch_to_cargo_and_write_their_log`; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:39; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:298-299) · `coverage` (`cargo llvm-cov` lcov to `target/coverage/lcov.info`, then its per-file report, then, chained since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, `python3 .github/scripts/coverage_floor.py` over three crate floors, the leg exiting with the floor's status; since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync both `cargo llvm-cov` lines take `--ignore-filename-regex 'keyboard_compat\.rs$'`, excluding dioxus-native-dom's crate-private `keyboard_compat.rs`, upstream's temporary keyboard-types 0.7/0.8 bridge, until escher takes upstream's retirement of it — `coverage_floor.py` and the three floors unchanged — pinned by `test_coverage_leg_reaches_the_floor_on_each_crate` (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:41-42; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:44-45;
 .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:330)) · `stand-repeat` (since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, not a fast leg: three rounds, each printing `stand-repeat: round R of 3` and running `cargo test -p blitz-tests --locked` with one `--test` per `tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_*.rs` and, on the same line, ten named blitz-tests targets outside that prefix as literal `--test` words, each file keeping its name (test-plan §9 → Legs names them), pinned by `test_stand_repeat_leg_runs_three_rounds` and read from the script's own text by `stand_requirement_sweep`'s leg check (test-plan §1),
 then `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked` over `cli_commands`, `cli_flow`, `host_binary`, `host_log`, `host_timer`, `mcp_server`, `mcp_log` and `recording`; the first red command ends the leg with its status — a zero-failure budget, no retry, no `--ignored`, no env var — and three green rounds end `stand-repeat: 3 of 3 rounds green`; the script reads the floor script and the `stand_*.rs` set beside itself, `SCRIPTS="$(dirname "$0")"`; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:48-65) · `fast` (fmt → clippy → test → ci-scripts, stopping at the first red: the local pre-push gate), every cargo leg `--locked` but `examples/wasm_hello` (no `Cargo.lock`); it tees the leg's merged output to `target/ci-logs/{leg}.log`, truncated at the leg's start, exits with the leg command's status, and prints the leg list to stderr and exits 2 on an unknown or missing leg (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:8-89); every ci.yml leg job ends with `actions/upload-artifact` (SHA-pinned, `# v7`) `if: failure()` named `ci-log-{job id}` (matrix `ci-log-matrix-{platform}`), uploading only its own log under `target/ci-logs/`, `retention-days: 7`, `if-no-files-found: ignore` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:48-54; .github/workflows/ci.yml:419-425); the `coverage` job alone also uploads `coverage-report` — `target/coverage/`, `if: success()`, `retention-days: 7` — the one fork-CI artifact outside `target/ci-logs/` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:286-291); the contract is pinned by `test_ci_workflows.py` (.github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:103-499);
 the package-install contract `bash .github/scripts/apt-install.sh [--attempts N] [--bound SECONDS] [--pause SECONDS] <package>...`, the one statement of fork CI's package install: up to 3 attempts, each `sudo timeout --kill-after=10 120 apt-get update` and then `apt-get install -y <packages>` under the same bound; a failed call — the bound's expiry included — prints one stderr line `apt-install: attempt {n} of {N} failed in {repair|update|install} (exit {status})`, pauses 10 s when another attempt remains, and the next attempt starts, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, with a bounded repair — `sudo timeout --kill-after=10 120 dpkg --configure -a`, phase `repair`, a failed repair failing that attempt — and then `update`, the first attempt running no `dpkg` (the operator's answer «Add a bounded repair» at that chunk's P4); exit grammar `0` an attempt completed · `1` every attempt failed · `2` usage — never the bound's own 124 or 137; its arguments are checked before any command runs — a package name must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9+.-]+$`, an option value `^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,5})$`, `--attempts` and `--bound` are at least 1, and at least one package is named; four constants at its head (`ATTEMPTS=3`, `BOUND=120`, `PAUSE=10`, and the kill grace `GRACE=10`, which no option sets), no environment variable of its own and no file written; ten `run:` steps of ci.yml call it (nine until 2026-10-14-quality-gates) with package names and no option, no leg of `ci-leg.sh` calls it and the dev host never runs it against a package manager; a bound that fires inside `apt-get install` can leave dpkg interrupted, which the next attempt's repair configures — no run has shown it on a real interrupted dpkg, the stand-in tests its one witness;
 it is pinned by `InstallScriptTest`, eight tests (five until 2026-10-14-quality-gates) that run it against a stand-in `sudo`, `apt-get` and `dpkg` with the real `timeout`, and by the workflow invariant `test_o_package_installs_are_bounded`, both in the `ci-scripts` leg (.github/scripts/apt-install.sh:17-73; .github/scripts/apt-install.sh:52-60; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:218-235; .github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:381-495) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-09-audit-corrections-agent-surfaces/report.md, the repair at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/report.md; the coverage-floor contract `python3 .github/scripts/coverage_floor.py LCOV CRATE_DIR=PERCENT …` (stdlib, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates): it sums `LF`/`LH` over every `SF` record whose real path, relative to the working directory, lies under each crate directory, prints one line per crate, `{dir} {hit}/{lines} = {pct:.2f} % (floor {f} %)`, then `coverage floor: N of N crates at or above their floors` (exit 0) or `coverage floor: K of N crates under their floors` (exit 1); a crate with no record exits 2 naming its directory on stderr and a malformed argument exits 2 with a usage line; it prints no source path but the crate directory and never echoes the lcov path; the `coverage` leg calls it with `packages/escher-driver=97 packages/dioxus-native-dom=83 packages/blitz-test-harness=90`; pinned by `test_coverage_floor.py` (`CoverageFloorTest`, 7 cases) and two `LegScriptTest` cases, in the `ci-scripts` leg (.github/scripts/coverage_floor.py:70-101; .github/scripts/test_coverage_floor.py:17-88);
 the agent-run test contract `bash scripts/agent-run.sh {boot | run {stand|all|name} | status | cleanup | logs}`, run from the repository root, drives `cargo test -p blitz-tests --locked` with exit grammar `0` success · `1` failed (an empty run included) · `2` usage, checked before · `3` precondition unmet, JSON-line events (`boot`, `run.start`, `test`, `run.end`, `status`, `cleanup`) encoded by an embedded python3 `json`, and state in `target/agent-run/` only — full contract in test-plan §3; `scripts/agent-run.ps1` is a pass-through Windows entry with no logic; pinned by `test_agent_run.py`, run by the existing `ci-scripts` leg (scripts/agent-run.sh:1-226; scripts/agent-run.ps1:1-4; .github/scripts/test_agent_run.py:88-266); the cold-agent run pipe `bash scripts/cold-agent.sh {run <task> | status | cleanup | logs}`, run from the repository root with the one task `stand` (since 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test; `counter` retired), follows the same grammar — exit `0` success · `1` a `failed` verdict · `2` usage, checked before any precondition · `3` precondition unmet (`claude` or `python3` not on PATH, `target/debug/escher-session` absent or not executable — one stderr line naming `cargo build --locked -p seven_guis --bin escher-session`, the pipe building nothing — no verdict, no `events.jsonl`) — with JSON-line events (`run.start`, `run.end`, `status`, `cleanup`) encoded by an embedded python3 `json` and state in `target/cold-agent/` only; `run` starts one isolated `claude -p` session (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-06) from a per-run `mktemp -d` directory with the fixed prompt `STAND_PROMPT` and only the escher server's twelve tools
 — the driver's own `escher-session mcp` (`--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, `--allowedTools mcp__escher`, `--setting-sources ""`, `--disable-slash-commands`, `--no-session-persistence`, `--model claude-opus-5-5`, `--max-budget-usd 3`, under `timeout 600`) — and writes `verdict.json` — `passed` only on positive evidence (client exit 0, a successful `result`, isolated — the twelve `mcp__escher__{verb}` tools, one server `escher` connected —, `counts_agree` between the server's `tool_call` span lines and the transcript, at least one tool call, all four lean apps met from the tool's own `snapshot` answers, and the agent's last fenced JSON check (≤ 65,536 bytes, ≤ 400 steps, closed keys and verbs) replayed passing on a fresh `escher-session mcp` child and failing on an ablated replay on a second), `wrong_calls` recorded and deciding nothing; the stub `scripts/cold_agent_stub.py` was deleted at 2026-10-15-cold-agent-test; `scripts/cold-agent.ps1` is a pass-through; pinned by `test_cold_agent.py` (a `claude` shim and a fake `escher-session`; no live model, credential or built binary), run by the existing `ci-scripts` leg — full contract in test-plan §3 (scripts/cold-agent.sh:13-29; scripts/cold-agent.sh:148-308; scripts/cold-agent.sh:450-482; .github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py:67-128; .github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py:200-222); the blitz-tests target contract — `[package]` does not set `autotests` to false, and the manifest holds exactly one `[[test]]` table, `all` at `tests/all.rs` with `test = false` — pinned by `test_blitz_tests_targets.py` (`BlitzTestsTargetsTest`, one test), run by the same leg, which discovers seven test files since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, six until then (.github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:17-26; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:56-59);
 root crate feature `log-times` = `log-frame-times` + `log-phase-times` forwarding to dioxus-native (Cargo.toml:265-268)

- **Unit:** blitz-tests
  - **Path:** tests/blitz-tests
  - **What it is:** Integration tests (tests/blitz-tests/lib.rs:1) covering accessibility (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:14; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:1-7) and, since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, the builder's three state attributes on a parsed page — every value of each grammar, on a role that supports the attribute and one that does not, `aria-checked` read on a checkable role alone and neither attribute on a native checkbox or radio, a 5,500-character `aria-checked` nowhere in the tree, 5 tests in both layout modes, run by the workspace test leg, per package and the `stand-repeat` leg (a named `--test` of its list), and not by the `a11y` CI leg, which runs six named files since 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, this one not among them (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_states.rs:134-316); the builder's merged `aria-expanded` · `aria-disabled` · `aria-level` reads, 3 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_merged_states.rs:88-157), the unread `aria-activedescendant` pinned, 1 test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_active_descendant_unread.rs:39-81), and an `inert` subtree skipped by Tab and Shift+Tab, passed through by a hit, absent from the tree and restored when `inert` is removed, the focus-fixup limit pinned, 4 tests (tests/blitz-tests/tests/inert_subtree.rs:68-194), each in both layout modes; block, inline, flex, grid, abspos/fixed and `display: contents` layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:1-7; tests/blitz-tests/tests/display_contents.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/oof_dynamic_cb.rs:1-5); inline text layout (tests/blitz-tests/tests/whitespace_modes.rs:15-25; tests/blitz-tests/tests/line_break.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_box_baseline.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/br_trailing_line.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inline_fragment_rects.rs:1-4);
 painting (tests/blitz-tests/tests/background_size.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/svg_background_size.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/outset_box_shadow_shape.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_order.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbars.rs:1-4); paint tree and hit testing, a hit past a node dropped since the last resolve included (tests/blitz-tests/tests/paint_tree_incremental.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pointer_events.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_test_dropped_nodes.rs:32-82); input (tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_events.rs:1-4; tests/blitz-tests/tests/touch_action.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:1; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_selection_anonymous_block.rs:1-8; tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:1-3); scrolling and fragment navigation (tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:1-2), and an into-view scroll through nested scrolling boxes with the visible-region reader — 7 tests, in both layout modes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scroll_into_view_nested.rs:1-10); a range input's default actions, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction — `range_input_interaction`, 8 tests on parsed pages (6 until 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep), each in both layout modes: the arrows, Home and End stepping a focused range input with one `input` per change, a click setting the value by position and focusing it, degenerate attributes keeping the value finite, bounded and on its grid, a decimal step reading its decimals, a disabled range input taking neither keys nor a click, and attribute writes re-seeding and re-sanitizing the value (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:117-302) and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, removing `value` re-seeding it, removing `step`, `min` or `max` re-sanitizing it, and a `type` change clearing the range data and a change back re-seeding it (tests/blitz-tests/tests/range_input_interaction.rs:304-409);
 a scrolled box's own geometry and the hit at a box that clips, since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit, each in both layout modes — `scrolled_box_client_rect`, 7 tests (a scrolled box's client rect, the nested case, the readers re-based on it and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, a `writing-mode: vertical-lr` box scrolled (70, 120) reading its unscrolled rect, green under both builds), `hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box`, 13 tests (a hit stopped at the padding box of a box that clips by `overflow`, the one-axis case, a `contain: paint` box stopping the hit at its padding box and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the hits at an `img`, inside an `iframe`'s sub-document and inside a filled text `input`, and a box both transformed and scrolled hit where its rows show) and `scrolled_box_absolute_position`, 1 test (a scrolled box's `Node::absolute_position` read where it stands) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_client_rect.rs:134-364; tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_clipped_at_scrolling_box.rs:187-400; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_absolute_position.rs:52-82); `transformed_client_rect`, 4 tests in both layout modes — a translated box, a scaled box and a translated parent's child read where their transforms move them while the child's offset rect does not, and a target inside a translated scrolling box reading outside its visible region (tests/blitz-tests/tests/transformed_client_rect.rs:79-220); style invalidation, transforms, units, transitions (tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/transform_2d_subset.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/rem_after_viewport_change.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:1-3); mutation and leaks (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inner_html_leak.rs:1);
 Dioxus integration (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:18-23; tests/blitz-tests/tests/harness_smoke.rs:102-113); `<link>` stylesheet loading (tests/blitz-tests/tests/link_rel_attribute.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:1-8); the seven_guis headless stand — mount, bundled-font text, fresh-boot and incremental identity, offline, one driven interaction per lean task, timer ticks, one stable element id per element (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_boot.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_counter.rs:1-2; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_flight_booker.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_timer.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_crud.rs:1-3; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:1-5); Dioxus falsy boolean-attribute clearing — `disabled` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_disabled.rs:1-6) and the 28 names of its own list on both attribute paths (the bridge's predicate upstream's 28-name `is_bool_attr` since 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship; `inert` the 28th name the check reads since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, the attribute half only — a truthy `inert` honoured — `inert_subtree`, `stand_keyboard` — and a falsy one cleared by the bridge), a falsy `hidden` leaving the element displayed and a snapshot node (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:1-8); the snapshot's per-control state through real input, and the password mask on an in-file fixture (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:1-10);
 the stand checks' shared module `tests/common/mod.rs` — no test target and no test in it, the one statement of the per-task tables `controls`, `tab_order`, `INPUT_NAMES` and `rendered` — joined at 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions by `ENABLED_TAB_ORDER` (the flight booker after `flight-return`, CRUD after a row is selected) and `REGION_NAMES` (`crud-list` → `People`) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:72-99; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:133-136) — and of seven helpers — `tab_order` (CRUD six stops, `crud-list` third) and the helper `focused` moved in from `stand_accessibility_ids` and `stand_snapshot_state` since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness — read through `mod common;` by 21 stand checks (`stand_contrast` the eighteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness, `stand_keyboard` the nineteenth, since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, and `stand_requirement_sweep` and `stand_non_lean_tasks` the twentieth and twenty-first, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep) (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:1-6; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:48-70; tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:101-121); since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness the stand keyboard check `stand_keyboard`, 14 tests in both layout modes (11 until 2026-10-14-stand-a11y-assertions, which added the last three and put it in the `a11y` CI leg) — Tab and Shift+Tab walking each lean task's stated sequence with wrap, the engine's focus, the snapshot's `focused` and the tree's focus agreeing at every step; Enter and Space on each focused stand button read as its click, 20 rows; the controls HTML gives the keys, a button disabled after it took focus and a button that is itself scrolled, on in-file fixtures; a click focusing each stand button; a `disabled` attribute skipping a form control by Tab and not a `<div disabled tabindex=0>`;
